For reference, these prayer clauses are enumerated herein under:
(a) Decree of possession in favor of the plaintiff and against the defendant no.1 and defendant no.2 jointly or separately in respect of suit portion the two rooms part of property no. H-34A contemplated in duly probated will dated 19.07.1991 vide order dated 04.01.2010 as specified and delineated above and more specifically shown in 'Red' in the site plan attached herewith;
(b) Decree of perpetual injunction thereby restraining the defendant no.1 and defendant no.2, their representatives and assignees from obstructing on any ground whatsoever in plaintiff carrying out construction of partition wall between part 'A' to 'A' as specifically shown in 'Blue' line in the plain attached for effecting proper partition wall upto maximum height of 15 Mtrs in the larger property for its equal division in two equal parts of one larger portion being H-34 A as shown in Blue and H-34 B also having equal land out of originally allotted CS DJ No.10367/16 Wanti Devi Vs. Ramswaroop Choudhary & Anr. Page no.7 of 33 Digitally signed by NAVJEET NAVJEET BUDHIRAJA BUDHIRAJA

(c) Decree of Rs.5,40,000/- (Rs. Five Lacs Forty Thousand Only) in favor of the plaintiff and against the defendant no.1 and 2 jointly or severally on account of mesne profit @ Rs.15,000/- per month for last three years;
Smt. Wanti Devi vs Shri Ramswaroop Choudhary on 9 February, 2023 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/32812940/
5 (d) Any other relief which this court may deem fit and proper in order to meet the ends of justice.

